# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
# Expansion 2026-11-20: new B2 sets (rank 5001-10000, or an OVERRIDE with its reason in select.py).

C('adem', "one adult in plain clothes, head and shoulders, seen from the side at the same distance, one hand resting flat on the chest, a plain wall behind, nose and mouth clearly visible. Only the small arrow at the hand on the chest changes, with the nose or mouth that goes with it.",
  "Ik adem in, houd mijn adem even in en adem dan uit.", "I breathe in, hold my breath for a moment and then breathe out.")
K('inademen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult seen from the side rests one hand flat on the chest, and the chest swells high under it; a small arrow at the hand points into the chest. Two short curved lines lead into the nostrils. The mouth is closed and the cheeks are flat.",
  "a hand on a swelling chest with a small arrow pointing in.",
  "fingers pinching the nose with no arrow (inhouden); a hand on a sinking chest with an arrow out (uitademen); a person blowing out a candle (uitblazen); a person smelling a flower (not the card).",
  "Pair with inhouden and uitademen. The only difference is the arrow at the chest: pointing in here, absent or pointing out there.",
  "adem ... in", "Ik adem rustig door mijn neus in.", "I breathe in calmly through my nose.", "heeft ingeademd",
  "Een volwassene met een hand op een rijzende borst zuigt lucht door de neus naar binnen.")
K('inhouden', "One drawing, one panel. An adult seen from the side rests one hand flat on a high, still chest and pinches the nose shut with two fingers of the other hand; the mouth is pressed shut, the cheeks flat, and no arrow or line shows anywhere.",
  "fingers pinching the nose and a hand on a still chest with no arrow.",
  "a hand on a swelling chest with an arrow in (inademen); a hand on a sinking chest with an arrow out (uitademen); a person filling an air mattress by mouth (blazen); a person with a hand over the mouth (not the card).",
  "Pair with inademen and uitademen. The only difference is the arrow at the chest: absent here, pointing in or out there.",
  "houd ... in", "Ik houd mijn adem even in.", "I hold my breath for a moment.", "heeft ingehouden",
  "Een volwassene knijpt met twee vingers in de neus en heeft een hand op een roerloze borst.")
K('uitademen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult seen from the side rests one hand flat on the chest, and the chest sinks low under it; a small arrow at the hand points out of the chest. The mouth hangs slack and open with no pursed lips, and two short lines leave it.",
  "a hand on a sinking chest with a small arrow pointing out.",
  "a hand on a swelling chest with an arrow in (inademen); fingers pinching the nose (inhouden); a person blowing out a candle (uitblazen); a person yawning (not the card).",
  "Pair with inademen and inhouden. The only difference is the arrow at the chest: pointing out here, pointing in or absent there.",
  "adem ... uit", "Ik adem langzaam door mijn mond uit.", "I breathe out slowly through my mouth.", "heeft uitgeademd",
  "Een volwassene met een hand op een zakkende borst duwt lucht door de slappe, open mond naar buiten.")

C('speelgoed', "two children sit on a plain floor facing each other, seen from the side at the same distance, one teddy bear between their hands, a plain wall behind. Only which way the teddy bear moves, pulled towards the left child or held out back to the right child, changes.",
  "Ik pak de knuffel van mijn broer af, maar ik geef hem snel terug.", "I snatch the teddy from my brother, but I quickly give it back.")
K('afpakken', "One drawing, one panel. The left child grabs the teddy bear out of the hands of the right child and pulls it towards their own chest, a small arrow pointing left; the hands of the right child stay open and empty and the mouth is open in protest.",
  "a teddy bear pulled from open hands towards the chest of the left child.",
  "the teddy bear held out back to the right child (teruggeven); a book slid back across a library counter (terugbrengen); a child picking a toy up from the floor (oprapen); a parcel handed over a counter (afhalen).",
  "Pair with teruggeven. The only difference is the teddy bear: pulled away from the right child here, held out back to the right child there.",
  "pak ... af", "Ik pak de knuffel van mijn broer af.", "I take the teddy away from my brother.", "heeft afgepakt",
  "Een kind trekt een knuffelbeer uit de handen van een ander kind naar de eigen borst.")
K('teruggeven', "One drawing, one panel. The left child holds the teddy bear out in both open hands towards the right child, a small arrow pointing right; the right child still has both arms stretched out from the snatch and an upset face, the mouth turned down.",
  "a teddy bear held out on open hands towards the other child.",
  "the teddy bear pulled away from the right child (afpakken); a book slid back to a librarian (terugbrengen); a gift offered across a table (aanbieden); bread passed along a row (doorgeven).",
  "Pair with afpakken. The only difference is the teddy bear: held out back to the right child here, pulled away from the right child there.",
  "geef ... terug", "Ik geef de knuffel aan mijn broer terug.", "I give the teddy back to my brother.", "heeft teruggegeven",
  "Een kind reikt een knuffelbeer op open handen aan een ander kind dat nog boos kijkt.")

C('poortje', "one adult in plain clothes passing through the open flaps of a waist-high ticket gate, seen from the side at the same distance, the station hall on the left and the platform with a train on the right, a plain card lowered in one hand. Only which way the adult walks through the flaps changes.",
  "Voor de reis check ik in en daarna check ik uit.", "Before the journey I check in and afterwards I check out.")
K('inchecken', "One drawing, one panel. The flaps of a waist-high ticket gate stand open and an adult walks through them from the hall towards the platform, face to the train, one foot past the flaps; a small arrow points right towards the train. A plain card hangs lowered in one hand, away from the reader.",
  "an adult stepping through the open gate flaps towards the train.",
  "the adult stepping through the flaps away from the train (uitchecken); a bank card held to a card terminal (pinnen); a person stepping into a bus (instappen); a person paying at a shop till (betalen); a person showing a ticket to a guard (not the card).",
  "Pair with uitchecken. The only difference is the way through the open flaps: towards the train here, away from it there.",
  "check ... in", "Bij het poortje check ik in.", "I check in at the gate.", "heeft ingecheckt",
  "Een volwassene loopt door de open klepjes van een poortje naar het perron met de trein.")
K('uitchecken', "One drawing, one panel. The flaps of the same ticket gate stand open and the adult walks through them from the platform towards the hall, back to the train, one foot past the flaps; a small arrow points left towards the hall. A plain card hangs lowered in one hand, away from the reader.",
  "an adult stepping through the open gate flaps away from the train.",
  "the adult stepping through the flaps towards the train (inchecken); a bank card held to a card terminal (pinnen); a person getting off a bus (uitstappen); a train arriving at a platform (aankomen); an adult walking out of a front door (weggaan).",
  "Pair with inchecken. The only difference is the way through the open flaps: away from the train here, towards it there.",
  "check ... uit", "Op het station check ik uit.", "I check out at the station.", "heeft uitgecheckt",
  "Een volwassene loopt met de rug naar de trein door de open klepjes van een poortje naar de hal.")

C('gordel', "one adult seated in the front seat of a plain car, seen from the side through the open door at the same distance, a seat belt across the seat, a steering wheel in front. Only where the belt lies, tight across the chest or hanging loose by the door, changes.",
  "Ik doe mijn gordel om en maak hem later los.", "I put on my seat belt and undo it later.")
K('omdoen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult in the driver's seat pulls the seat belt across the chest and clicks it into the clip beside the hip, a small arrow pointing into the clip. The belt is the mark: a broad band lying flat and tight from shoulder to hip.",
  "a broad belt lying tight across the chest from shoulder to hip.",
  "the belt hanging loose by the door (losmaken); a person putting on a coat (aantrekken); a rope tied round a post (vastbinden); a person stepping into a bus (instappen).",
  "Pair with losmaken. The only difference is the belt: tight across the chest here, hanging loose by the door there.",
  "doe ... om", "In de auto doe ik mijn gordel om.", "In the car I put on my seat belt.", "heeft omgedaan",
  "Een volwassene in een auto heeft de autogordel strak over de borst en klikt hem in de sluiting.")
K('losmaken', "One drawing, one panel. An adult in the driver's seat has just pressed the clip beside the hip, and the belt is the mark: a broad band hanging loose and slack beside the door pillar, off the chest, a small arrow pointing away from the clip.",
  "a broad belt hanging loose by the door, off the chest.",
  "the belt tight across the chest (omdoen); a person untying a rope from a post (losbinden); a cable pulled from a laptop (loskoppelen); a person taking off a coat (uittrekken).",
  "Pair with omdoen. The only difference is the belt: hanging loose by the door here, tight across the chest there.",
  "maak ... los", "Bij aankomst maak ik mijn gordel los.", "On arrival I undo my seat belt.", "heeft losgemaakt",
  "Een volwassene in een auto drukt op de sluiting en de autogordel hangt slap naast de deur.")

C('bibliotheek', "a plain library counter seen from the side at the same distance, a librarian standing behind it on the left, a visitor in front of it on the right, shelves of plain book spines behind, one closed book. Only which way the book crosses the counter changes.",
  "De bibliotheek leent het boek uit en ik breng het terug.", "The library lends the book and I bring it back.")
K('uitlenen', "One drawing, one panel. The librarian behind the counter starts to slide a closed book towards the visitor, the book still at the near edge under the flat hand of the librarian; a small arrow points right, towards the visitor. A short stack of books stands at the elbow of the librarian.",
  "a book under the hand of the librarian at the near edge, arrow to the visitor.",
  "the visitor sliding the book back across the counter (terugbrengen); a teddy bear held out back to a child (teruggeven); a parcel handed over at a post counter (afhalen); a gift offered in both hands (aanbieden).",
  "Pair with terugbrengen. The only difference is the direction of the book: from the librarian to the visitor here, from the visitor to the librarian there.",
  "leent ... uit", "De bibliotheek leent ook tijdschriften uit.", "The library also lends out magazines.", "heeft uitgeleend",
  "Een bibliothecaris heeft de hand op een gesloten boek en schuift het naar een bezoeker.")
K('terugbrengen', "One drawing, one panel. The visitor in front of the counter starts to slide a closed book towards the librarian, the book still at the visitor's edge under the flat hand of the visitor; a small arrow points left, towards the librarian. The stack of books at the elbow of the librarian is unchanged.",
  "a book under the hand of the visitor at the far edge, arrow to the librarian.",
  "the librarian pushing the book to the visitor (uitlenen); a teddy bear held out back to a child (teruggeven); homework handed in to a teacher (inleveren); a person posting a parcel (opsturen).",
  "Pair with uitlenen. The only difference is the direction of the book: from the visitor to the librarian here, from the librarian to the visitor there.",
  "breng ... terug", "Ik breng het boek op tijd terug.", "I bring the book back on time.", "heeft teruggebracht",
  "Een bezoeker heeft de hand op een gesloten boek op de balie en schuift het naar de bibliothecaris.")

C('tafel', "a plain kitchen table seen from the side at the same distance, one adult standing at it, a plain cupboard behind with its door open, four plain plates and four cups. Only which way the plates move, down onto the table or up off it in a stack, changes.",
  "Ik zet de borden klaar en ruim na het eten de tafel af.", "I set out the plates and clear the table after the meal.")
K('klaarzetten', "One drawing, one panel. An adult at the table sets the last of four clean plates down in front of an empty chair, three plates and three cups already in place round the table; a small arrow points down to the table. The cupboard door behind is open.",
  "the last clean plate going down into a row of laid places.",
  "a stack of used plates lifted off the table (afruimen); a chair tucked in at the table (terugzetten); a plate lowered in front of a guest (serveren); plates washed at a sink (afwassen).",
  "Pair with afruimen. The only difference is the plates: going down onto the table here, coming off it in a stack there.",
  "zet ... klaar", "Ik zet de borden alvast klaar.", "I set out the plates in advance.", "heeft klaargezet",
  "Een volwassene legt een schoon bord op een tafel waar al drie borden en drie kopjes staan.")
K('afruimen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult at the same table lifts a stack of four used plates with crumbs and a cup on top off the table, the places bare round it; a small arrow points up from the table. The cupboard door behind is open.",
  "a stack of used plates lifted off a bare table.",
  "a clean plate set down into a laid place (klaarzetten); toys tidied into a box (opruimen); a chair carried away from the table (weghalen); a table wiped with a cloth (schoonmaken).",
  "Pair with klaarzetten. The only difference is the plates: coming off the table in a stack here, going down onto it there.",
  "ruim ... af", "Na het eten ruim ik de tafel af.", "After the meal I clear the table.", "heeft afgeruimd",
  "Een volwassene pakt een stapel vuile borden met kruimels van een lege tafel.")

C('vaatwasser', "a plain dishwasher with its door down and the lower rack pulled out, seen from the side at the same distance, one adult crouching beside it, a plain shut cupboard above. Only which way a plate moves, from a dirty stack in the arm down into the rack or up out of the rack onto a clean stack, changes.",
  "Ik ruim de vaatwasser in en later ruim ik hem uit.", "I load the dishwasher and later I unload it.")
K('inruimen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult crouches at an open dishwasher and holds a stack of dirty plates in the crook of one arm and lowers the top one into an empty slot of the pulled-out rack, a small arrow pointing down into the slot. The rack is half full.",
  "a dirty plate lowered into a slot of the pulled-out rack.",
  "a clean plate lifted out of the rack (uitruimen); plates washed by hand in a sink (afwassen); a plate dried with a towel (afdrogen); boxes loaded into a van (inladen).",
  "Pair with uitruimen. The only difference is the plate: going down into the rack here, coming up out of it there.",
  "ruim ... in", "Na het eten ruim ik de vaatwasser in.", "After dinner I load the dishwasher.", "heeft ingeruimd",
  "Een volwassene met een stapel vuile borden op de arm zet een bord in het rek van een open vaatwasser.")
K('uitruimen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult crouches at the same open dishwasher and holds a stack of clean, shining plates in the crook of one arm and lifts one more up out of a slot of the pulled-out rack, a small arrow pointing up out of the slot. The rack is half full.",
  "a clean shining plate lifted up out of the rack.",
  "a dirty plate lowered into the rack (inruimen); a plate dried with a towel (afdrogen); boxes lifted out of a van (uitladen); things taken out of a suitcase (uitpakken).",
  "Pair with inruimen. The only difference is the plate: coming up out of the rack here, going down into it there.",
  "ruim ... uit", "Elke ochtend ruim ik de vaatwasser uit.", "Every morning I unload the dishwasher.", "heeft uitgeruimd",
  "Een volwassene met een stapel schone borden op de arm haalt een glanzend bord uit het rek van een open vaatwasser.")

C('fiets', "one adult in plain clothes beside a plain bicycle on a flat street, seen from the side at the same distance, both hands on the handlebars, a low wall behind. Only which way the leg of the adult swings over the saddle, up onto the bike or down off it, changes.",
  "Ik stap op en bij de bakker stap ik weer af.", "I get on and at the baker's I get off again.")
K('opstappen', "SKIP: getting on and getting off a bike pass through the same poses, so the two stills differ only in the arrow, and any honest cue (which foot is down, the lean of the bike, the rider rising or sinking) changes more than one element.",
  "a leg swinging up over the saddle with the other foot still on the ground.",
  "a leg coming back down over the saddle to the ground (afstappen); a person stepping into a bus (instappen); a person riding fast (not the card); a person standing still on a pavement (stilstaan).",
  "Pair with afstappen. The only difference is the swinging leg: going up over the saddle onto the bike here, coming back down over it to the ground there.",
  "stap ... op", "Na het stoplicht stap ik weer op.", "After the traffic light I get back on.", "is opgestapt",
  "Een volwassene heeft de handen aan het stuur van een fiets en zwaait een been over het zadel.")
K('afstappen', "SKIP: set with opstappen, for the reason given there.",
  "a leg coming back down over the saddle towards the ground.",
  "a leg swinging up over the saddle onto the bike (opstappen); a person getting off a bus (uitstappen); a child dropping from a bar (loslaten); a person falling off a bike (not the card).",
  "Pair with opstappen. The only difference is the swinging leg: coming back down over the saddle to the ground here, going up over it onto the bike there.",
  "stap ... af", "Bij de brug stap ik af.", "At the bridge I get off.", "is afgestapt",
  "Een volwassene laat een been over het zadel van een fiets naar de grond zakken.")

C('rits', "one adult in a plain jacket with a long zip, seen from the front at the same distance, waist up, one hand on the zip pull, a plain wall behind. Only which way the zip pull moves, up to the chin or down to the waist, changes.",
  "Ik rits mijn jas dicht en binnen rits ik hem weer open.", "I zip up my coat and indoors I unzip it again.")
K('dichtritsen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult in a plain jacket pulls the zip pull up to the chin with one hand, the jacket closed from the waist to the neck, the other hand holding the bottom of the zip; a small arrow points up along the zip.",
  "a zip pull drawn up to the chin over a closed jacket front.",
  "the zip pull drawn down with the jacket opening (openritsen); a coat being put on over the shoulders (aantrekken); a bag being packed (inpakken); a seat belt clicked into its clip (omdoen).",
  "Pair with openritsen. The only difference is the zip: pulled up to the chin with the jacket closed here, pulled down with the jacket opening there.",
  "rits ... dicht", "Buiten rits ik mijn jas dicht.", "Outside I zip up my coat.", "heeft dichtgeritst",
  "Een volwassene trekt het lipje van een jas omhoog tot onder de kin.")
K('openritsen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult in the same plain jacket pulls the zip pull down towards the waist, the two halves of the jacket parting above it to show a plain shirt; a small arrow points down along the zip. The other hand holds the edge of the jacket.",
  "a zip pull drawn down with the jacket halves parting above it.",
  "the zip pull drawn up to the chin (dichtritsen); a coat being taken off at the elbows (uittrekken); a suitcase being unpacked (uitpakken); a door swung wide (opendoen).",
  "Pair with dichtritsen. The only difference is the zip: pulled down with the jacket opening here, pulled up to the chin with the jacket closed there.",
  "rits ... open", "Binnen rits ik mijn jas open.", "Indoors I unzip my coat.", "heeft opengeritst",
  "Een volwassene trekt het lipje van een jas omlaag en de twee helften wijken uit elkaar.")

C('bad', "one plain bathtub with a tap at the left end and a plug hole, seen from the side at the same distance, a plain wall behind, a towel on a rail. Only the water changes: pouring in from the tap, or swirling out down the plug hole.",
  "Het bad loopt vol en na het baden loopt het weer leeg.", "The bath fills up and after the bath it empties again.")
K('vollopen', "SKIP: its partner leeglopen is dropped (Bijvoeglijke naamwoorden owns leeggelopen), and no separable verb that one visible change tells apart is left to pair with.",
  "a stream from the tap and a half-full tub with an upward arrow.",
  "water swirling down the open plug hole (leeglopen); a hand turning a tap (opendraaien); a glass being filled (not the card); a person in the bath (not the card).",
  "Pair with leeglopen. The only difference is the water: pouring in from the tap here, swirling out down the plug hole there.",
  "loopt ... vol", "Het bad loopt langzaam vol.", "The bath slowly fills up.", "is volgelopen",
  "Uit de kraan stroomt water in een half gevuld bad met de stop erin.")
K('leeglopen', "SKIP: duplicate of Bijvoeglijke naamwoorden leeggelopen (owner ruling 20 November: the adjective keeps the word).",
  "a spiral swirl at the open plug hole with a downward arrow.",
  "water pouring in from the tap (vollopen); a tap being turned off (dichtdraaien); a bucket emptied into a sink (not the card); a flat bicycle tyre (not the card).",
  "Pair with vollopen. The only difference is the water: swirling out down the plug hole here, pouring in from the tap there.",
  "loopt ... leeg", "Het bad loopt heel langzaam leeg.", "The bath empties very slowly.", "is leeggelopen",
  "Het water in een bad draait in een kolk naar het open afvoergat en de stop ligt ernaast.")

C('tribune', "a row of three spectators in plain clothes on a low stand at the edge of a plain sports field, seen from the front at the same distance, one player running with a ball on the field in front of them. Only the arms and mouths of the spectators change.",
  "Eerst moedigt het publiek de speler aan, daarna jouwt het hem uit.", "First the crowd cheers the player on, then it boos him.")
K('aanmoedigen', "One drawing, one panel. Three spectators on a low stand raise both arms high and shout with broad open smiles towards the player on the field, short burst lines round their hands; the player runs with the ball below them.",
  "three spectators with arms raised high and broad open smiles.",
  "spectators with thumbs down and frowning shouts (uitjouwen); a player sitting on a bench watching (toekijken); a team lifting a cup (winnen); a party with balloons (vieren); a person waving goodbye (not the card).",
  "Pair with uitjouwen. The only difference is the spectators: arms up and smiling here, thumbs down and frowning there.",
  "moedig ... aan", "Ik moedig mijn zus luid aan.", "I cheer my sister on loudly.", "heeft aangemoedigd",
  "Drie toeschouwers steken lachend hun armen omhoog naar een speler op het veld.")
K('uitjouwen', "One drawing, one panel. Three spectators on the same low stand hold their thumbs down towards the player on the field and shout with wide frowning mouths, short jagged lines coming from them; the player runs with the ball below them.",
  "three spectators with thumbs down and wide frowning mouths.",
  "spectators with arms raised and smiling (aanmoedigen); a person shouting into a phone (not the card); a person looking away (wegkijken); a player stepping onto the pitch (invallen).",
  "Pair with aanmoedigen. The only difference is the spectators: thumbs down and frowning here, arms up and smiling there.",
  "jouwt ... uit", "Het publiek jouwt de speler uit.", "The crowd boos the player.", "heeft uitgejouwd",
  "Drie toeschouwers steken boos hun duimen omlaag naar een speler op het veld.")

C('luchtbed', "one adult in plain clothes kneels beside a half-flat air mattress on a plain floor, seen from the side at the same distance, the valve at the near corner, a plain wall behind. Only what fills the mattress changes: the mouth of the adult at the valve, or a foot pump with a hose.",
  "Ik blaas het luchtbed niet op, ik pomp het op.", "I don't blow up the air mattress, I pump it up.")
K('opblazen', "SKIP: its partner oppompen is dropped (Bijvoeglijke naamwoorden owns opgepompt), and blowing up by mouth alone is the Werkwoorden blazen picture.",
  "puffed cheeks with the lips round the mattress valve.",
  "a foot pump with a hose on the valve (oppompen); a person blowing out a candle (uitblazen); a person holding the breath with puffed cheeks (inhouden); a person asleep on the mattress (not the card).",
  "Pair with oppompen. The only difference is what fills the mattress: the mouth of the adult at the valve here, a foot pump with a hose there.",
  "blaas ... op", "Ik blaas het luchtbed helemaal op.", "I blow up the air mattress completely.", "heeft opgeblazen",
  "Een volwassene heeft de lippen om het ventiel van een half leeg luchtbed en bolle wangen.")
K('oppompen', "SKIP: duplicate of Bijvoeglijke naamwoorden opgepompt (owner ruling 20 November: the adjective keeps the word).",
  "a foot pump pressed down with its hose on the mattress valve.",
  "lips round the valve with puffed cheeks (opblazen); a bicycle tyre being pumped (not the card); a foot on a car pedal (not the card); a balloon being tied (not the card).",
  "Pair with opblazen. The only difference is what fills the mattress: a foot pump with a hose here, the mouth of the adult at the valve there.",
  "pomp ... op", "Ik pomp het luchtbed snel op.", "I pump up the air mattress quickly.", "heeft opgepompt",
  "Een volwassene trapt op een pedaal met een slang naar het ventiel van een half leeg luchtbed.")

C('pasta', "one adult in plain clothes at a plain kitchen counter, seen from the side at the same distance, a pan of cooked pasta in the hands, a sink with a colander on the left and an empty plate on the right. Only where the pasta goes, into the colander or onto the plate, changes.",
  "Ik giet de pasta af en schep hem daarna op.", "I drain the pasta and then I serve it up.")
K('afgieten', "One drawing, one panel. An adult tips a pan of cooked pasta over a colander in the sink, a stream of water and pasta pouring into it and steam rising, water running out of the holes of the colander below; a small arrow points down into the sink. The plate on the counter stays empty.",
  "a tipped pan pouring pasta and water into a colander in the sink.",
  "pasta spooned from the pan onto a plate (opscheppen); a person pouring coffee (not the card); a sieve shaken over a bowl (not the card); dishes washed in a sink (afwassen).",
  "Pair with opscheppen. The only difference is where the pasta goes: into the colander in the sink here, onto the plate there.",
  "giet ... af", "Ik giet de pasta voorzichtig af.", "I carefully drain the pasta.", "heeft afgegoten",
  "Een volwassene kiept een pan met pasta en water boven een schaal met gaatjes in de spoelbak.")
K('opscheppen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult holds the same pan of cooked pasta tilted over the plate on the counter and lifts a heap of pasta onto it with a large spoon, a little steam rising; a small arrow points down onto the plate. The colander in the sink stays empty.",
  "a large spoon lifting pasta from the pan onto the plate.",
  "pasta and water poured into a colander (afgieten); a person eating up a plate of food (opeten); a plate set down at a laid table (klaarzetten); a stew stirred on a stove (not the card).",
  "Pair with afgieten. The only difference is where the pasta goes: onto the plate here, into the colander in the sink there.",
  "schep ... op", "Ik schep voor iedereen pasta op.", "I serve up pasta for everyone.", "heeft opgeschept",
  "Een volwassene legt met een grote lepel pasta uit een pan op een bord.")
